{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on `3474623c`, XD-1: option (c), in three steps, so that no\ngate is lost to a case that the harness hid until today.\n\nThe finding matters more than the log lines. A Native test or hook\nthat passes its limit does not fail. So a hang can pass the gate.\n\n1. Name the crossings first. The setup file guards the abort, so\n   that `onTimeout` cannot throw. In this step a crossing prints one\n   line with the file, the test or hook, and the limit, and the test\n   continues as it does today. The gate summary counts the lines.\n   This rides the C4 head as its own commit, and the C4 gate names\n   every crossing at no cost.\n2. Repair each named case. A case that is fast alone and slow only\n   beside other files takes the existing deadline factor. A case\n   that is slow alone moves to the scale tier by the GS-1 route.\n   State the alone time of each case in the note.\n3. Make a crossing fail. This lands in the head after the first\n   gate that counts zero crossings.\n\nConditions:\n- One paired control in the harness's own test: a case with a\n  limit of 1 ms must print the line in step 1, and must fail in\n  step 3. Without the setup file, the same case shows the lost\n  timeout.\n- The note names the versions that the guard depends on\n  (`@vitest/runner` 4.1.12 and the pool), so that an upgrade\n  checks whether the guard is still needed.\n- Say if the Plain project can lose a timeout in the same way. I\n  read your stack as Native only.\n\nYour item 4 stands as an inference: no product code calls the\nthrower, and no deployed Worker was tested. I accept that.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}